<title>JAPAN: Japan trust banks announce capital adequacy ratios.</title>
<headline>Japan trust banks announce capital adequacy ratios.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's seven major trust banks on Monday disclosed their capital adequacy ratios and unrealised profits on shareholdings as of March 31, the end of the 1996/97 business year.</p>
<p>Capital adequacy ratios were as follows (with year-earlier comparisons):</p>
<p>			     MARCH 1997    MARCH 1996</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Trust	 9.68 pct     10.23 pct</p>
<p> Sumitomo Trust	   8.96 pct	9.00 pct</p>
<p> Mitsui Trust	     9.56 pct     10.82 pct</p>
<p> Yasuda Trust	     9.86 pct     10.79 pct</p>
<p> Toyo Trust		10.02 pct	9.85 pct</p>
<p> Chuo Trust		 9.11 pct     10.52 pct</p>
<p> Nippon Trust	    11.23 pct	8.70 pct</p>
<p>Unrealised profits on shareholdings as of March 31, 1997 were as follows (in billions of yen, with year-earlier comparisons):</p>
<p>					 MARCH 1997	 MARCH 1996</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Trust		    541.1		828.6</p>
<p> Sumitomo Trust			313.1		627.3</p>
<p> Mitsui Trust			  375.5		767.2</p>
<p> Yasuda Trust			   40.77	     279.20</p>
<p> Toyo Trust			    168.0		323.5</p>
<p> Chuo Trust			     62.3		132.7</p>
<p> Nippon Trust			   21.0		 37.0</p>
<p>The seven trust banks are Mitsubishi Trust &amp; Banking Corp, Sumitomo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd, Toyo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd, Chuo Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd, Nippon Trust Bank Ltd, Mitsui Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd and Yasuda Trust &amp; Banking Co Ltd.</p>
</text>
